<section class="panel">
    <h2>What is Classic+?</h2>
    <p>Classic+ is the community's term for a new expansion of WoW Classic — new zones, raids, classes and systems layered on the Vanilla world instead of a re-release. Blizzard's China-only <strong>Titan Reforged</strong> (level-80 Vanilla/TBC/Wrath merge) is widely read as the working prototype, and datamined store licenses point to an internal project codenamed <strong>Project Camelot</strong>, expected to be revealed at <a href="https://blizzcon.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BlizzCon 2026</a> (Sept 12-13, Anaheim).</p>
</section>

<section class="panel">
    <h2>What We Know About Project Camelot</h2>
    <p>All evidence is not equal. Here is what has actually been observed versus what remains theory.</p>
    <h3>Observed — datamined & tracked</h3>
    <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Project Camelot naming in Blizzard's backend information</li>
        <li>An encrypted WoW 1.60 development branch</li>
        <li>Heroic and Epic licensing references</li>
        <li>Updates across multiple development environments</li>
        <li>A brief vendor-environment appearance</li>
        <li>Development advancing to Patch 1.60.1</li>
        <li>Encrypted promotional assets under investigation</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Interpretation — what the activity may indicate</h3>
    <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Camelot is receiving continued development</li>
        <li>Blizzard is maintaining more than one test branch</li>
        <li>The project may involve a substantial WoW product</li>
        <li>Some development activity may relate to Classic infrastructure</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Unconfirmed — rumors & community theories</h3>
    <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Project Camelot is WoW Classic Plus</li>
        <li>Dwarf Shamans will become playable</li>
        <li>Shen'dorei or Skyborne Elves are a new race</li>
        <li>The game will remain permanently at level 60</li>
        <li>A beta or BlizzCon demo is imminent</li>
        <li>Any rumored release date or feature list</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="meta-info">Compiled from <a href="https://quissy.tv/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">QuissyTV's Camelot evidence tracker</a>.</p>
</section>

